    "title": "When does 'Euphoria' season 3 come out? Date, time, how to watch",
    "text": "Updated April 7, 2026, 1:42 p.m. ET\"Euphoria\" fans are days away from learning what happens next for Rue, Cassie, Nate and Jules.The new season, set five years after season 2, is scheduled to premiere on HBO on April 12. A trailer, released by HBO on March 30, gave fans a glimpse into the characters' futures and what to expect in season 3.Here's what to know about \"Euphoria\" season 3.Watch the official trailer for 'Euphoria' season 3When does 'Euphoria' season 3 come out?April 12.What time does 'Euphoria' season 3 come out?9 p.m. ET April 12 on HBO.How many episodes are in season 3?8.Do you need an HBO subscription to watch 'Euphoria'?Yes, viewers need a paid HBO subscription to watch \"Euphoria,\" including the upcoming season 3.HBO Max subscription plans start at $10.99 per month with ads, while the standard ad-free subscription costs $18.49 per month.The highest tier, which is $22.99 a month, includes the ability to stream on four devices and offers 4K Ultra HD video quality and 100 downloads. HBO also offers bundles with Hulu and Disney+.What happens in 'Euphoria' season 3?In season 3, Rue Bennett (Zendaya) is in Mexico, in debt to Laurie (Martha Kelly) and trying to \"come up with innovative ways to pay it off,\" creator Sam Levinson said during an HBO presentation Dec. 3. Cassie Howard (Sydney Sweeney) and Nate Jacobs (Jacob Elordi) are engaged and living in the suburbs.Jules Vaugn (Hunter Schafer) is in art school, and Maddy Perez (Alexa Demie) is a talent agency manager in Hollywood.'Euphoria' season 3 castZendaya, Sweeney, Elordi, Schafer and Demie will return for season 3.Some new faces, Levinson said, include Kelly, Sharon Stone, Spanish singer-songwriter Rosalía, Danielle Deadwyler, Darrell Britt-Gibson and former NFL player Marshawn Lynch. Natasha Lyonne, Trisha Paytas, Eli Roth and Homer Gere will also make their \"Euphoria\" debuts, according to Levinson.Will Eric Dane be in 'Euphoria' season 3?Yes. Eric Dane returned to the \"Euphoria\" set one last time for his role as Cal Jacobs, the father of Nate Jacobs (Jacob Elordi).Dane made his \"Euphoria\" return in the latest trailer for season 3.The actor died Feb. 19 at 53, nearly one year after he announced his diagnosis of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, or ALS. According to People magazine, Dane had filmed his scenes for the upcoming season before his death.What is 'Euphoria' about?Released on HBO in 2019, \"Euphoria\" is, or rather was, about a group of high school students struggling with drugs, sex and identity. The series is both an American adaptation of the Israeli show of the same name and an ode to Levinson's own experiences with drug abuse. \"Euphoria\" has received more than 40 awards since its debut, including nine Emmys.",
